WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.134
More breaking news tonight.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.202
In fact, it is a moment.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.703
59 years in the making.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:04.771
The National Archives

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.438
tonight has released

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.639
more than 13,000

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.575
documents related to the 1963

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.542
assassination of President

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.343
John F Kennedy.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.611
The second of two releases

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.646
ordered last year by President Biden

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.314
extraordinary

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.448
because of the subject matter

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.483
as well as the decades

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.517
it's taken to finally see

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.418
these documents.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.419
The CIA tonight

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.453
says it has now released

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.488
all information known

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.555
to be related directly

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.790
to the assassination

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.259
with about 95% of all agency documents

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.794
within the JFK Assassination

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.062
Records Collection Act.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.164
Now public in their entirety.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:31.931
CNN's Tom Foreman

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.900
joins us with more on this milestone.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.668
What do we know about these documents

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:36.036
so far?

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:36.636
Well, we know,

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.670
first of all, as you noted,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.672
there are a lot of them Anderson.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.242
This is the equivalent of a dozen copies

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.577
of War and Peace being dumped out there.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.679
And yet this is a tiny fraction

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.315
of the roughly 5 million documents

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.851
related to the JFK assassination.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.953
We also know, based on what

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.255
some JFK assassination

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.489
historians have said,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.690
what the CIA has said, what

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.358
other people shown,

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.526
what history has shown

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.928
that what we're not likely to find in

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.431
this is any kind of giant breakthrough,

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:07.100
some really smoking gun explanation here

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.468
as to how this happened.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.869
Or some secret conspiracy,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.638
nothing that will satisfy

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.139
the conspiracy theorists out there.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.040
That said,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.809
there are a lot of interesting details

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.010
here, Anderson. Like what?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.211
What have you found so far?

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:18.745
Well,

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.346
a lot of it has to do with the process

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.515
of how the CIA goes about things.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.317
Some of that explains partially

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.852
why this has been hidden for so long.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.387
So it doesn't reveal their methods,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.421
how they surveilled

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.123
people down in Mexico.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.458
Soviet people down there

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.393
had secret wiretaps down there.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.527
At one point,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.929
there is a small line

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.098
where a psychologist of some sort

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.966
who had looked at Oswald,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.534
Oswald was cited as saying

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.036
Oswald's motivation

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.170
is largely explained

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.040
in terms of his neurotic background,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.141
his failure

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.075
to achieve status

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.643
and his very deep resentment

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.112
of all authority.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.580
Oswald saw a movie on TV

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.447
about an attempted

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.615
presidential assassination

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.349
with a rifle

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.317
shortly before his death,

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.752
which could have sparked him into action.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.321
So there are explanations like that

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.956
which would totally point

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.858
toward Oswald as acting alone.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.493
But then there's another one

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.360
where they talk about

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.795
an intercepted phone call

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.530
between Cuba and Miami

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.131
two days

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.533
after the assassination of the president.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.503
The gist of which was Plan of Castro

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.171
carried forward.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.472
Bobby is next.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.441
Obviously a reference to Bobby Kennedy,

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.276
who indeed was killed five years later.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.811
Soon the atomic bombs will reign

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.546
and they will not know from where.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.480
This, however,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.648
although that would light up

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.350
a conspiracy theorist.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.485
There is no indication in this record

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.620
that the CIA

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.221
or anyone else took this very seriously.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.723
This was like the talk of a blowhard.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.457
It seemed like

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.291
if anything, they said,

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.125
well, it's a good lesson

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.093
in how people can be listening

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.361
in on your phone calls.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.396
You don't expect a lot of that in here.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.798
And is everything released now or

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.499
I mean, it seems like there

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.134
still may be some more stuff out there.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.169
No, there is still

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:50.803
some material out there

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.238
and not a whole lot.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.640
It's a it's a small amount.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.707
The collection,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.109
according to the archives,

00:02:56.109 --> 00:03:00.580
still has 515 documents withheld in full.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.384
Another 2545 withheld in part.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.586
I'm not entirely clear

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.954
when or how the rest of

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.023
it will be released, but again,

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.591
there's just no indication

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.892
that what is hiding

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.828
there is some great revelation.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.197
But what could be hiding?

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.432
There is even more information

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.300
about the details

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.768
of how things were handled,

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.336
how it was investigated,

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:26.606
and maybe something that will put rest

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.807
some of these conspiracies,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.642
although after all these years Anderson.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.710
I wouldn't bet on it.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.978
Yeah. Tom, thank you.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.079
I keep going through the documents.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.080
Fascinating perspective

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.647
now from CNN

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.449
presidential historian Tim Naftali.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.584
Tim, how big a deal is this?

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.687
Well, Anderson,

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:44.624
it's a huge deal that our government

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:48.394
basically is forcing our intelligence

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.929
community to release things

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.698
they never wanted to release.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.533
Remember, this is the fourth

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.735
or fifth bite at the Apple

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.637
that the intelligence community had.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.240
And the first few go arounds

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.341
the intelligence community kept

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.942
arguing for national security reasons.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.311
We can't release these details

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.615
And the combination of Trump's conspiracy

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:09.549
thinking

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.417
and Joe Biden's

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.052
determination for transparency

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.053
has led to this day

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.722
where we have documents

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.657
that have no redactions at all,

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.392
which talk about very sensitive

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.827
CIA operations

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.328
that have nothing to do

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.997
with the assassination of JFK.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.098
But everything to do

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:25.932
with the secret world

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.668
of the 1960s and seventies.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:29.636
Does anything in the files

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.204
change the official

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.171
historical record

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.140
and conclusion about JFK assassination

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.843
Now, I don't think nothing.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.878
I mean, I have to say

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.714
this was described as ten worn pieces

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:43.016
I couldn't possibly get through.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.217
One War and Peace

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.085
in the course of an afternoon

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.220
I sampled

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.421
based on some assumptions

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.857
I had about what might be out there.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.592
About 10% of the material.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.693
I didn't see anything

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.827
nor was expecting anything

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.130
to change the main narrative that

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.533
Lee Harvey Oswald was a self-radicalizing

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:01.734
assassin.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.603
We had had a number of them before

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.337
in our history.

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.038
And of course,

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:06.039
if you think about the history

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:07.340
of Islamist terrorism,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.675
a lot of it involved

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:10.143
self-radicalized individuals.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.211
So that basic narrative doesn't change.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.247
But here's the crux of it all.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.717
One of the reasons we have conspiracy

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.218
theories to the extent

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:22.622
we do in our culture, is that after World

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.089
War Two,

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.391
we created a national security state

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:28.461
that introduced layers of secrecy

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.796
in our own government.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:30.930
That meant that our own government,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.531
for reasons

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.499
it felt reasonable

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.269
couldn't always tell us what it was doing

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.204
abroad and at times at home,

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.672
that was secrets

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.941
layered upon secrets, layer upon secrets,

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:44.010
led to an explosion of

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.012
skepticism in this

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.814
country in the seventies,

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.415
a series of investigations

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.917
and then shocked Americans

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.819
about what our government was up to

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.487
We've never recovered

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.022
from that shock to our basic

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.057
trust in government to this day.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.592
Now, I think it's worse now than it's

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.893
been since the seventies.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.061
But if you want to see

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.329
why Americans thought

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:05.064
their government was overly secretive,

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.133
take a look at some of these details,

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.068
give you a few examples.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:09.502
The U.S.

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:10.403
government

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.572
illegally was intercept

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.774
getting our letters.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:15.508
That's not a

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.210
that that became known in the seventies,

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.011
but they were intercepting letters

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:19.912
of pretty prominent

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:20.713
people like Jane

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.749
Fonda in the 1970s

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:25.518
Tom Hayden and Jane Fonda sued the U.S.

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:26.853
government to get access

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.321
to their FBI materials

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:29.722
that had not been released

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.290
in the Freedom of Information

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.626
Act requests they had made to the FBI.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.660
They lost.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.128
Well today

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:38.464
we know that the CIA had intercepted

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.633
four letters that were sent to MS.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:43.302
Fonda in the year 72 73,

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:44.804
and then

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:45.471
she wouldn't and

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.907
wouldn't release them to her.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.342
It gives you an example of sort

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:51.978
of the level of surveillance

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:52.612
that our government

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:54.347
was engaged in that period.

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:56.449
So I think people will understand

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:58.985
now a bit about the culture of secrecy

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.787
that developed in the Cold War

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:02.221
and why there was a huge pitch

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.623
back in the seventies, and again

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:05.792
there was a huge push back after nine 11.

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:06.826
And one reason

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:08.728
why we should be very worried

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.696
about unrestrained

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:11.664
and unrestrained

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:12.698
national security community.

